    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0559" n="273" xml:id="pg273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.622a/150</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-13T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3086. Your 3978, June 9, noon. <hi rendition="#italic">China</hi> correspondence
                    will be made public as soon as believed expedient.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d361-f1"
                    />
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d361-f1" n="1" xml:id="d361-f1-content">
                <p>It was excluded from the volume, <hi rendition="#italic">European War No. 3,
                        Diplomatic Correspondence with Belligerent Governments relating to Neutral
                        Rights and Duties</hi>, printed and distributed by the Department of State
                    in August 1916, and remained unpublished, with the exception of the telegraphic
                    instructions of February 23, 1916, to the Ambassador in Great Britain and the
                    British note of March 16, 1916 (<hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg632">pp. 632</ref>, <ref target="#pg633">633</ref>), which had
                    already been released in April.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
